{"name":"Baked Bean","hex":"#b2754d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked bean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single bean in a portion of baked beans.","baked beans"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked_bean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baked beans","blocks":[{"text":"Baked beans are a dish traditionally containing white common beans that are parboiled and then baked in sauce at low temperature for a lengthy period. Canned baked beans are not baked, but are cooked through a steam process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Baked_beans_in_tomato_sauce.jpg/330px-Baked_beans_in_tomato_sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baked_beans","wikidata":"Q804297"},{"title":"Baking","blocks":[{"text":"Baking is a method of preparing food that uses dry heat, typically in an oven, hot ashes, or on hot stones. The most commonly baked foods in 2025 were bread and rolls. Heat is gradually transferred from the surface of unbaked goods to their center, typically at elevated temperatures surpassing 300 °F. Dry heat cooking imparts a distinctive richness to foods through the processes of caramelization and surface browning. As heat travels through, it transforms batters and doughs into baked goods and more with a firm dry crust and a softer center. Baking can be combined with grilling to produce a hybrid barbecue variant by using both methods simultaneously, or one after the other. Baking is related to barbecuing because the concept of the masonry oven is similar to that of a smoke pit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/330px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking","wikidata":"Q720398"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Beanpots.jpg/500px-Beanpots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Beanpots.jpg/500px-Beanpots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Three beanpots used for cooking homemade baked beans. The small one is glazed with the letters \"Boston Baked Beans\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeanpots.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg/500px-Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg/1280px-Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg/500px-Commoner_lunch_%28Pilaki_in_a_can%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th